.TITLE "kill"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Sends a signal to a process, usually to __terminate__ it. It is used to stop unresponsive programs or manage background tasks by their __Process ID (PID)__.

.DIV "TLDR"
**kill pid**
Sends the default termination signal (TERM) to a process.
> __pid__ the Process ID of the target

**kill -9 pid**
Forcefully kills a process immediately, preventing it from performing any cleanup.
> __-9__ kill signal flag | __pid__ the Process ID

**kill -l**
Lists all available signals that can be sent to a process.
> __-l__ list signals flag

**killall name**
Kills all processes that match a specific program name instead of using a PID.
> __name__ the name of the program to stop

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Always try a standard __kill__ first, as it allows the program to save data and close correctly. Use __kill -9__ only as a last resort for programs that are completely frozen and unresponsive to normal signals.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:ps** **linux:top** **linux:pkill**

